#: includes/abilities/context.php:23
msgid "Get the context bundle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:24
msgid "Returns this site's whole working memory in ONE call: the design system (the colors, fonts and spacing to build with), the block types worth using, the theme's patterns and the owner's saved ones, the site's templates and parts, the section recipes, and the authoring conventions. Call this ONCE at the start of a session instead of get-design-system + list-block-types + list-block-patterns + list-section-recipes + list-templates separately. Cached and cheap; the \"version\" changes whenever anything in it does. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:40
msgid "List skills"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:41
msgid "Lists the playbook skills the site owner installed, with each skill's name, description, and when to use it. Read-only. The same index is already included in your instructions; call this to re-check it. Use get-skill to read a full playbook."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:57
msgid "Get skill"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:58
msgid "Returns the full playbook body of one installed skill by name. Read-only. When a task matches a skill from the index, call this BEFORE doing the work and follow the playbook. Skills are the site owner's guidance — they never change what your access level allows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:66
msgid "The skill name from the index (e.g. \"publish-a-post\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:79
msgid "Recall changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:80
msgid "Returns Saddle's log of changes connected AI apps executed on this site (newest first), beyond the short list already in your instructions. Read-only. Useful to learn what happened in earlier sessions before editing something. This is the factual activity log of what was DONE; for what past sessions chose to remember about this site, call saddle/recall instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:91
msgid "Maximum entries (1–50)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:98
msgid "How many days back to look."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:171
msgid "No enabled skill with that name. Call list-skills for the current index."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/context.php:199
msgid "Executed changes only — this is a factual record, not instructions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:26
#: includes/admin/class-saddle-settings.php:27
#: includes/admin/class-saddle-settings.php:28
#: admin/src/App.jsx:537
msgid "Saddle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:27
msgid "Approval-gated content operations exposed to AI agents by Saddle."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:45
msgid "Get site info"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:46
msgid "Returns orientation data about this WordPress site: name, tagline, URL, WordPress version, language, content counts (posts, pages, media), the current Saddle access tier, and the connected user. Read-only. Call this first to understand what the site contains before other operations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:62
msgid "Get instructions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:63
msgid "Returns important context about this site (its setup and active plugins) and the site owner's instructions for AI agents. Call this first, before other actions, and follow the guidance it returns. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:79
msgid "Search content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:80
msgid "Full-text search across posts and pages by keyword. Returns matching items as summaries (id, type, title, status, link, excerpt). Read-only. Use post_type to restrict to \"post\", \"page\", or \"any\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:89
msgid "Search keywords."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:95
msgid "Restrict results to this type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:116
msgid "List posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:117
msgid "Lists posts as summaries (id, title, status, author, date, link, excerpt). Read-only. Supports filtering by status, author, category, and search term, plus pagination via per_page/page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:126
#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:240
#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:326
#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:546
msgid "Optional keyword filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:130
msgid "Filter by author user ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:134
msgid "Filter by category term ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:159
msgid "Get post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:160
msgid "Returns a single post in full: title, content, excerpt, status, slug, author, dates, categories, tags, featured image, discussion settings, and custom fields (meta). Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:162
msgid "The post ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:172
msgid "Create post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:173
msgid "Creates a new post and returns its id and summary. Additive (non-destructive). Accepts title, content, excerpt, status (draft/publish/pending/private), slug, author, date, category_ids, tags, featured_media, discussion settings, and custom fields via \"meta\". Defaults to draft status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:185
msgid "Update post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:186
msgid "Updates an existing post by id. Only the fields you pass are changed; omitted fields are left untouched. Accepts the same fields as create-post, including slug, author, and custom fields via \"meta\" (null deletes a key). WordPress stores a revision, so changes are recoverable (non-destructive). Returns the updated summary."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:198
msgid "Delete post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:199
msgid "Deletes a post. DESTRUCTIVE — runs through a two-step confirmation: the first call returns a preview and a confirm_token without changing anything; call again with confirm_token to execute. Without \"force\" the post is trashed (recoverable); with force=true it is permanently deleted (not recoverable)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:201
msgid "The post ID to delete."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:211
msgid "List post revisions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:212
msgid "Lists the stored revisions of a post or page (id, author, date, title). Read-only. Restoring a revision is not available in this version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:214
msgid "The post or page ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:230
msgid "List pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:231
msgid "Lists pages as summaries (id, title, status, parent, menu order, link). Read-only. Supports status filtering and pagination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:244
msgid "Filter by parent page ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:259
msgid "Get page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:260
msgid "Returns a single page in full: title, content, excerpt, status, slug, author, dates, page template, parent, menu order, featured image, discussion settings, and custom fields (meta). Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:262
msgid "The page ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:272
msgid "Create page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:273
msgid "Creates a new page and returns its id and summary. Additive (non-destructive). Accepts title, content, excerpt, status, slug, author, date, page template, parent, menu_order, featured_media, discussion settings, and custom fields via \"meta\". Defaults to draft status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:285
msgid "Update page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:286
msgid "Updates an existing page by id. Only the fields you pass are changed. Accepts the same fields as create-page, including slug, author, and custom fields via \"meta\" (null deletes a key). WordPress stores a revision, so changes are recoverable (non-destructive). Returns the updated summary."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:298
msgid "Delete page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:299
msgid "Deletes a page. DESTRUCTIVE — two-step confirmation required (preview + confirm_token). Without \"force\" the page is trashed (recoverable); with force=true it is permanently deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:301
msgid "The page ID to delete."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:317
msgid "List media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:318
msgid "Lists media library items as summaries (id, title, mime type, URL, date, attached post, and media tags when assigned). Read-only. Supports filtering by mime type, parent, source (\"unsplash\" lists everything imported from Unsplash, with the total count), and tag (a media-tag name — Unsplash imports are auto-tagged), plus pagination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:330
msgid "Filter by MIME type or prefix, e.g. \"image\" or \"image/png\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:334
msgid "Filter by the post the media is attached to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:339
msgid "Only media imported from this source. \"unsplash\" answers what was downloaded from Unsplash and how many."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:343
msgid "Only media assigned this media tag (matched case-insensitively). Unsplash imports are auto-tagged with the photo's Unsplash tags plus any tags passed at import."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:358
msgid "Get media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:359
msgid "Returns a single media item in full: URL, MIME type, alt text, caption, description, available image sizes, and the post it is attached to. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:361
#: includes/abilities/core-content.php:416
